{
  "fixture": "headers/model-000NN-of-00062.safetensors.header.json (62 files)",
  "fixture_form": "BYTE-IDENTICAL COPY of each shard's safetensors header, data excluded",
  "source_url_form": "https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash/resolve/04c4e9e95c5da8862dced7e5056455116f83a7e0/model-000NN-of-00062.safetensors",
  "upstream_repo": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash",
  "upstream_revision": "04c4e9e95c5da8862dced7e5056455116f83a7e0",
  "how_fetched": "two HTTP range GETs per shard, both answered 206: bytes 0-7 for the little-endian u64 header length N, then bytes 8..8+N-1 for the header itself, written verbatim. NO weight byte was requested. The hub's own x-linked-size was then read with a HEAD and compared to 8 + N + max(data_offsets end) for every shard.",
  "why_these_land": "inc-glm53f-022 part 2 serves the whole model weights-free, and the CPU-compile start's loader reads real shard headers rather than deriving shapes from the config. These headers let the host build 62 header-true, data-sparse shards with no network of its own and about 6 MB of real disk.",
  "how_the_host_uses_them": "each shard is rebuilt as the 8-byte little-endian N, then these header bytes verbatim, then a hole to computed_size via truncate -s. The header digest, the resulting size and the allocated block count are all wanted.",
  "holds_weights": false,
